Original commit body from 3d7165e76eedf72e0d8343dc7a5a144066497e70:

C linked a function value everywhere but at file scope: `int (*G)(void) =
glob;` and `= &adr;` emitted nothing. C++ linked only `&f` and call
arguments: a designated field ({ .run = f }), a pointer variable, an
assignment, a return and an array of function pointers had no edge, and
its static dispatch tables' dispatches_to edges started at a table symbol
C++ never emitted (C's WI-dirij, unported) -- finalize dropped them (apt:
6 tables).

Shared in core analyze/c_family (C, C++ and CUDA import it):
- c_family_is_value_operand: an initialiser, a plain `=` right side, a
  return operand, an aggregate element -- not a callee, argument, target,
  operator operand or compound assignment (zstd `ip += ZSTD_frameHeaderSize`).
- c_family_array_declarator (moved from c.py): the array through the
  function / parenthesized / pointer wrappers an array of function pointers
  adds.
- c_family_declares_local / c_family_file_scope_variables: a parameter,
  local, range-for variable (apt `for (auto const& Arch : Archs)`), local
  enumerator, C++ template parameter (x265 `template<int size>`) or file-scope
  VARIABLE of the name (zstd's `static const size_t ZSTD_frameHeaderSize = 4;`
  beside a ZSTD_frameHeaderSize() elsewhere) shadows the function. A
  prototype -- a pointer return too (`void *nk_malloc(...)`) -- is no
  variable; a name the file defines is never one (zstd's macro-wrapped
  `void *myalloc _Z_OF((...));`). Computed once per file, and only after the
  name resolves to a function, so the arm costs ~1% (haproxy + x265: 54.5 s
  vs 53.9 s).

C: a value arm (initialisers, assignments, returns) anchored on the file at
file scope; file-scope `&f` now anchors there too. Initializer lists stay
with the dispatch-table pass.

C++: the same arm plus positional and designated aggregate elements; array
tables stay with the dispatch pass, which now unwraps pointer arrays and
emits the table symbol (post_process). A bare name names a free function,
never a member (C++ spells one `&C::m`). In code tree-sitter misread -- an
ERROR with no clean definition between, a definition nested in another (C++
has none), a `public:` read as a statement label, a file-scope block -- no
bare value is taken: apt's export-macro classes (`class APT_PUBLIC
pkgCacheFile`) parse as functions whose inline accessors sit beside the data
members they shadow, and had bound `return Cache;` / `return Origin;` /
`OldMetaIndex->Origin = Origin;` to them (35 edges, all wrong). In member
context (a method, an X::f definition, a class body) only this file's
function is taken; cost: x265's `hpelcomp = sad;` (a template in another
file) is not linked.

